><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FURUKAWA HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IKEDA KAZUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SEKIGUCHI TOMOKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ARAI, TOSHIAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FURUKAWA, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IKEDA, KAZUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEKIGUCHI, TOMOKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An I/O bus signal for reporting occurrence of a trouble of an I/O bus is sent to an I/O bus manager from a manager at a predetermined timing. The I/O bus manager initializes the I/O bus and notifies the CPU of the computer of the I/O bus trouble as an interruption to be processed by the OS on which the CPU is running. Even if an I/O bus trouble occurs, trouble information can be acquired after the interruption by the OS.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Selon cette invention, un signal de bus E/S destiné à signaler la présence de perturbations du bus E/S est envoyé depuis un gestionnaire à des intervalles prédéterminés à un gestionnaire de bus E/S. Le gestionnaire de bus E/S initialise le bus E/S et signale à l'UC de l'ordinateur la perturbation du bus E/S sous la forme d'une interruption devant être traitée par le système d'exploitation qui tourne dans l'UC. Même en cas d'une perturbation du bus E/S, les informations sur cette perturbation peuvent être obtenues après l'interruption par le système d'exploitation.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>